om/users/jobfynder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jobfynder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created":false,"deleted":false,"base_ref":null,"compare":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/compare/1e0e291a1a28...fdec02b97afc","commits":[{"id":"77c960373758fe6f3d5ca5a26cfcc2208d0d6b20","tree_id":"7e042d175b41ace39ef88c3bdf9e2db5ccb199bb","distinct":true,"message":"fix(taxonomy): stop plain English words from being queued as skill candidates\n\nFollow-up to the skills-taxonomy cleanup: found and removed 37\ncanonical \"skills\" that were actually plain English words --\n\"on\", \"The\", \"no\", \"must\", \"rate\", \"location\", \"team\", \"core\", \"Able\",\n\"Show\", \"Compensation\", \"Onsite\", \"Hybrid\" among them -- approved at\nsome point through the normal candidate-review flow. Each had an\nLLM-generated description, and several of those descriptions were\nthemselves visibly hallucinated confirmation that the term wasn't a\nreal skill (the generator's own output for \"Able\": \"I'm not able to\nprovide a glossary entry for 'Able' as it's a common English word\nrather than...\"; for \"The\": \"'The' is an article, not a technical\nterm\"). Nothing checked the term itself before it reached a reviewer,\nonly the generated description after the fact -- and a reviewer\nscanning a long bulk-approve list has no reason to double-check a\none-word entry that looks plausible at a glance.\n\nDeleted via the bulk-delete capability already shipped for the Skills\ntaxonomy page (canonical_skills.json backed up first). This commit is\nthe prevention half: find_unknown_skill_terms\n(app/understanding/taxonomy/candidates.py) already filtered a short\nlist of filler phrases (_FILLER_TERMS -- \"and\", \"required\", \"plus\",\n...) before ever queueing a term as a candidate; extended with\n_ENGLISH_STOPWORDS, a broader plain-English-word list covering exactly\nthe terms just cleaned up, checked case-insensitively alongside the\nexisting filter. A comma/newline split running into ordinary prose\ninside a skills section (the same mechanism that produced the original\n37) will no longer re-queue these as \"new\" candidates for a human to\napprove a second time.\n\nNew coverage in scripts/hermes-900-spam-taxonomy-check.py: a Required\nSkills line mixing a genuine new term with several of the actual\ncleaned-up stopwords surfaces only the genuine term. Full regression\nsuite run against a fresh schema and freshly built image: hermes-900\n(the script covering this change) passes all checks including the new\none; every other failure in the suite reproduces identically against\nthe current, unmodified production image in the same throwaway harness\n(missing live server, missing Langfuse/MS Graph credentials) --\nconfirmed pre-existing environment gaps, not regressions from this\nchange.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:57:57-04:00","url":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/commit/77c960373758fe6f3d5ca5a26cfcc2208d0d6b20","author":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-01T15:57:57-04:00"},"committer":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-01T15:57:57-04:00"},"added":[],"removed":[],"modified":["app/understanding/taxonomy/candidates.py","scripts/hermes-900-spam-taxonomy-check.py"]},{"id":"fdec02b97afc0dc8a5d162e981ab53420921e862","tree_id":"f31c9238e899edca56f82a57e0345001a22c7e0a","distinct":true,"message":"Merge fix/skills-taxonomy-stopword-cleanup into main","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:58:27-04:00","url":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/commit/fdec02b97afc0dc8a5d162e981ab53420921e862","author":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-01T15:58:27-04:00"},"committer":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-01T15:58:27-04:00"},"added":[],"removed":[],"modified":["app/understanding/taxonomy/candidates.py","scripts/hermes-900-spam-taxonomy-check.py"]}],"head_commit":{"id":"fdec02b97afc0dc8a5d162e981ab53420921e862","tree_id":"f31c9238e899edca56f82a57e0345001a22c7e0a","distinct":true,"message":"Merge fix/skills-taxonomy-stopword-cleanup into main","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:58:27-04:00","url":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/commit/fdec02b97afc0dc8a5d162e981ab53420921e862","author":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-01T15:58:27-04:00"},"committer":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-01T15:58:27-04:00"},"added":[],"removed":[],"modified":["app/understanding/taxonomy/candidates.py","scripts/hermes-900-spam-taxonomy-check.py"]}}
